\paragraph{Multi-seed stability.}
Across 5 random seeds, 7--8B models show stable probe performance (precision std ${<}4$pp, balanced accuracy std ${<}3$pp). R1-32B exhibits high variance (precision std $= 12.8$pp, FPR std $= 14.5$pp), consistent with the narrow operating window ($W{=}1$ only) and small sample ($n{=}20$). This supports a two-tier framing: 7--8B results constitute robust evidence, while 32B results are pilot-scale with model-specific caveats.

\paragraph{Joint hyperparameter selection.}
Layer, window size $W$, and detection threshold are all selected on the same validation set (20\% of traces; $n{=}4$--$9$ at 32B). Regularization insensitivity ($C$-sweep yields ${<}2$pp variation) partially mitigates overfitting risk, but does not eliminate it. Nested cross-validation would be ideal but is impractical at $n{=}19$--$20$.

